1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:10,340
Right now, somewhere in Brazil, a kid is drawing giant sparkly eyes in a school notebook.

2
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:19,573
In Paris, someone is dressed as a ninja on the subway. In Manila, a whole family is arguing about which anime to watch tonight.

3
00:00:19,973 --> 00:00:28,700
Most of these stories come from one country: Japan. So how did a small island nation become the anime capital of the world?

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:38,556
Our story begins in nineteen seventeen, in Tokyo, when movies were silent and storytellers called benshi spoke over the films.

5
00:00:38,956 --> 00:00:45,229
That year, a few young artists drew the very first Japanese cartoons by hand, frame by frame.

6
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:55,252
One that still survives is called Namakura Gatana, The Blunt Sword. It is about a samurai who buys a terrible sword and loses every fight.

7
00:00:55,652 --> 00:00:58,832
It lasts about two minutes. Making it took months.

8
00:01:00,132 --> 00:01:07,472
After the war, a young doctor named Osamu Tezuka decided he would rather draw comics than treat patients.

9
00:01:07,872 --> 00:01:14,273
He filled his manga with movie tricks: close-ups, dramatic angles, and big, expressive eyes.

10
00:01:14,673 --> 00:01:21,736
Fans called him the God of Manga, and editors sometimes waited outside his door all night for his pages.

11
00:01:23,036 --> 00:01:32,552
Meanwhile, in nineteen fifty-eight, the studio Toei released The Tale of the White Serpent, one of Japan's first full-length color animated films.

12
00:01:33,852 --> 00:01:40,872
Then, on New Year's Day, nineteen sixty-three, Tezuka's Astro Boy flew onto Japanese television.

13
00:01:41,272 --> 00:01:51,001
A weekly cartoon was very expensive, so his team got clever. They reused drawings, moved only the mouths, and slid pictures across the screen.

14
00:01:51,401 --> 00:02:00,491
This cheaper style, called limited animation, became part of the anime look. Sometimes, being short on money is the mother of invention.

15
00:02:00,891 --> 00:02:05,457
Just eight months later, Astro Boy was flying on American TV too.

16
00:02:06,757 --> 00:02:10,087
Here is Japan's secret ingredient: manga.

17
00:02:10,487 --> 00:02:18,083
Weekly comic magazines tried out thousands of stories, readers voted for their favorites, and the winners got to move.

18
00:02:19,383 --> 00:02:25,571
In the nineteen eighties, home video arrived, and creators made bolder stories for older fans.

19
00:02:25,971 --> 00:02:34,399
In nineteen eighty-eight, Akira roared onto movie screens, and audiences overseas realized cartoons were not just for kids.

20
00:02:35,699 --> 00:02:41,247
Then came the nineties, and a little yellow electric mouse took over playgrounds everywhere.

21
00:02:41,647 --> 00:02:50,331
Kids traded cards at lunch, sang the theme song, and tried to catch them all, while parents tried to figure out what a Pokemon even was.

22
00:02:51,631 --> 00:02:58,224
In two thousand three, Hayao Miyazaki's Spirited Away won the Oscar for Best Animated Feature.

23
00:02:58,624 --> 00:03:05,388
A Japanese film about a girl working in a bathhouse for spirits had won one of Hollywood's biggest prizes.

24
00:03:06,688 --> 00:03:11,105
Today, anime streams to fans in almost every country on Earth.

25
00:03:11,505 --> 00:03:18,504
In two thousand twenty, Demon Slayer: Mugen Train became the highest-grossing film ever in Japan.

26
00:03:18,904 --> 00:03:31,385
And in twenty twenty-three, Japan's anime industry earned about three point three trillion yen, more than twenty billion US dollars, and over half of it came from fans outside Japan.

27
00:03:32,685 --> 00:03:39,108
So why Japan? First, the stories: manga gave anime a giant library of ideas.

28
00:03:39,508 --> 00:03:46,144
Second, the style: artists learned to do a lot with a little, and created a look anyone can recognize.

29
00:03:46,544 --> 00:03:55,911
And third, anime was never only for kids. There is a story for everyone: robots, romance, sports, cooking, and even volleyball.

30
00:03:57,211 --> 00:04:02,225
Back in Brazil, the kid finishes the drawing and flips the corner of the notebook.

31
00:04:02,625 --> 00:04:05,507
The little doodle in the margin starts to move.

32
00:04:05,907 --> 00:04:09,257
And just like that, the next anime story begins.
